 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Causa con из-за",
   "texto": [
    "**Из-за + genitivo** means «for / because of»: **из-за пробки**, **из-за дождя**. It usually appears in the face of an obstacle or an unfavourable result, but the nuance depends on the context.",
    "**Мы опоздали из-за пробки** (we're late for the jam)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Case with sentence: так как",
   "texto": [
    "**Так как** and **потому что** enter a full sentence and express cause. **Так как** may appear at the beginning, as here: **Так как была авария, все стояли** (since there was an accident, all were standing). There is no fixed difference in formality between the two connectors.",
    "**Поскольку** also expresses cause («since», «since»)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common favourable cause: благодаря",
   "texto": [
    "**Благодаря + dativo** means «thanks to» and usually presents a favourable cause: **благодаря тебе**, **благодаря друзьям**. The contrast with **из-за** is a trend, not an absolute rule."
   ]
